Date: Sat, 13 Sep 2025 03:16:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix app launch issue by adding missing @AndroidEntryPoint
 to DeepLinkActivity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Added @AndroidEntryPoint annotation to DeepLinkActivity for proper Hilt DI
- Moved MainActivity to correct package location (app/src/main/java/com/anpan/app/)
- Created missing theme files (Color.kt, Typography.kt, Theme.kt) in core/designsystem
- Created AnpanNavigation.kt for app navigation structure
- Created MainScreen.kt with Japanese bottom navigation tabs (ホーム, ソーシャル, ウォレット, AI, チャット)
- Updated Kotlin version to 1.9.20 for Compose Compiler compatibility
- Fixed AndroidManifest.xml with proper activity declarations
- Added required resource files (strings.xml, colors.xml, backup_rules.xml)

Fixes app startup crash caused by missing Hilt annotation on DeepLinkActivity
that is declared in AndroidManifest.xml but lacks proper DI configuration.
App now launches successfully to main screen with bottom navigation.

Co-Authored-By: mizumin@ymail.ne.jp <mzmz0402@yahoo.co.jp>
